> for profit, but it does require that you also make its "source" (i.e.
> the JPEG files?) available under the terms of the NGPL.
>
> More seriously, the project is arguably a derivative work of D&D
> (Sceptre of Might), Edmund Spenser (Magic Mirror of Merlin),  Robert E.
> Howard (Heart of Ahriman), and Jack Vance (Eyes of the Overworld).
> NetHack is evidently too minor to warrant those copyright holders
> pursuing it for infringement, and the fact that it is distributed for
