Yeah. Selling fanfiction for profit is not really allowed - e.g. I
couldn't sell my own writings about Tolkien characters for profit (not
that I've done any), but it seems to be OK to post them on the web
freely. Although my pictures are derivatives of a derivative work
itself, it looks like selling for profit is looking increasingly
unlikely.

Which is really really annoying because the profit isn't the motive. I
just want to be able to get nicely bound and printed characters. I can
have a free PDF calendar with the appropriate images made up, but that
wouldn't be nearly as nice because it'd require people to get it
printed and bound themselves.

Bah humbug. The real world exists to crush my dreams. Yep, just mine,
it's only biased against me in particular :P

The other way to do it is to just do a calendar *without* any of the
names on. e.g. just call each of the images by a general name -
"Amulet" "Eyes" "Heart"... but then if you refer back and see that the
image was originally called "Nethack - The Heart of Ahriman" or
whatever, then it could still be argued that there was violation of
various licenses.

It's looking like the only way to do this is to provide a free PDF
calendar myself. And perhaps links to companies that'll print/bind it.
That way, no profit is being made, no-one is selling anything and all
licensing is happy.

Still sucks though. Means that if you want a nice version of it, you'll
have to find somewhere to get it printed/bound yourself.

